   the built Born number 256 x 56169 / 65773 = 218.6196; the exact cos^2(22.5 deg) x 256 = 218.5097; the pinned count 219 (DETECTOR)
   the rung keeps 219 iff the plus weight >= 28742801/512 = 56138.283, a margin of 30.717 on the weight (0.1196 of a cell)
   the shift per unit weight w on the class +-3: 46565 on the weight, 181.24 cells of 1 / 256
   w* (the polariser) = 15727/23841280 = 0.000660 = 1 / 1516: above it the reading is 218, not 219; below it the reading is 219
   the chain's cell 0+: Born 3154956561 of 4326087529 (256 x = 186.6973, the pinned 187); the class +-3 92236816; w* (the chain) = 0.001089 = 1 / 919
   the margin-free bound (a shift of one whole cell, whatever the margin): w = 65773 / (46565 x 256) = 0.005518 = 1 / 181.2
   the class +-1 mod 8 (j = 7, 9, 15, 17, 23, 25, 31): the same weights as j = 1 at 22.5, 45 and 90 degrees; Malus bounds nothing on it

6. THE TWO-SLIT BANDS (L2b; DETECTOR: the bright pixels 19 to 51 clicks of 4096 births, the rungs within one; paper main.tex line 1204)
   the member j reads 1 + cos(2 pi j D / 64) where Born reads 1 + cos(2 pi D / 64); a weight w on j != 1 moves a pixel's count by at most
   w x |cos(j t) - cos(t)| x (peak / (1 + V)) <= 2 w x 51 / 1.966 = 51.9 w clicks (V = 0.966 the registered visibility); one click is the cell, so
   a change of one whole click needs w >= 1 / 51.9 = 0.0193; below that the bands cannot be relied on to exclude it (the pixels' margins not read here)
